{"kind":"promise","text":"Promised. Recutting onto current main 4d5d62b6, docs-only, exactly the two fixes and no more.\n\nNote the order: I ratified your report fdb48b25 at the act above BEFORE filing this promise, rather than reading the answer and moving straight to the work. That is the standing rule I set myself after fdb55923, and this is the first row it applies to.\n\nOn fix 1, I want to state what I got wrong rather than just what I will change. Your original conditions said hermeticGitEnvironment's GIT_CONFIG stripping is defense-in-depth, not a defended boundary. I put that helper inside a paragraph asserting that where the code bounds the environment anyway it is buying determinism rather than defence. That is not a softened version of your condition; it is its opposite, written into the one document whose job is to say what is and is not defended. Codex's security reasoning is the part that matters: describing the helper as determinism erases a control that exists, and the next maintainer who reads it has been told it is safe to weaken the signing and verification quarantine. I will describe internal/app's bounding as determinism and hermeticGitEnvironment's stripping as a defended control, and keep the two visibly separate rather than in one paragraph.\n\nOn fix 2, codex found something I had not seen at all. My sentence said an attacker who can set these variables can already run code as the operator. Some of those variables route or select configuration rather than naming a program, and whether code runs at all depends on there being a relevant Git invocation. I wrote the sweeping version because it made the paragraph read cleanly, which is a bad reason to widen a security claim.\n\nI will recut rather than reuse 802a7c31 even though it still merges clean, re-derive the page's bases at filing, run full gates including internal/docset, publish a fresh artifact at the changed doc path, and request independent review. I will not merge, and I will tell you when the recut head is live so 2996e429 can be retired onto this child without stranding the commit."}